# Explore before Grep/Read

> **ABSOLUTE**: For structural code questions — how something works, call paths, blast radius, architecture, "where is X", "who calls Y" — call **`ax_explore`** (or `ax_search` / `ax_node` / graph tools) **before** broad `Grep` / `Read` sweeps. Skipping this is a protocol violation and tanks MCP quality (`ExploreBeforeGrep`).

`GetMcpTools` / schema discovery is **not** explore. You must call `ax_explore` (or another graph tool) in the same turn before repo-wide Grep/Read.

## Why

Graph answers usually replace many file reads. One `ax_explore` + targeted `ax_node` / `ax_callers` beats a dozen Greps. Agents that open with repo-wide Grep/Read burn tokens and weaken the quality score.

## Required order

```text
1. ax_preflight   [once per turn]
2. ax_explore / ax_search / ax_node / ax_callers / …
3. Read / Grep only for files the graph already pointed to
```

Treat numbered source returned by `ax_explore` as already read — do not re-Grep the same symbols.

## Filling gaps — stay in the graph

| The graph answer… | Do this | Not this |
|---|---|---|
| shows a snippet marked `truncated` | `ax_node` on that symbol — full source (up to 400 lines) plus direct callers and callees | Read the file |
| ends with an `[ax context cache]` footer | `ax_expand` with the footer id and offset | Read the files it named |
| missed the symbol you need | `ax_search` / `ax_node` with the exact name; `ax_sync` if the file changed | repo-wide Grep |
| needs who-calls / what-breaks | `ax_callers` / `ax_callees` / `ax_impact` | Grep for the name |

Where the graph covers the code, do not Read or Grep the file to fill the gap. `ax_node` is the full source of a symbol, served from the index.

## Allowed Grep/Read without explore

- Opening a file path the user explicitly named
- Reading a file right before you edit it (the editor needs exact current text)
- Files the graph does not index: config, lockfiles, docs, generated output, logs
- MCP unreachable (Mode: DEGRADED) — then Grep/Read is fallback; say so

## Forbidden

- Starting structural investigation with repo-wide Grep/Read while ax MCP is available
- Re-deriving architecture that `ax_explore` / `ax_insights` already indexes
- Using Grep to discover call paths when `ax_callers` / `ax_callees` / `ax_impact` exist
- Treating `GetMcpTools` as a substitute for `ax_explore`
- Reading a whole file to see a function `ax_node` can return
